## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to take ownership under time pressure, address bias ethically, and balance customer impact with product experimentation.

## Key Concepts

- Ownership and accountability in cross-functional triage
- Bias detection, containment, and mitigation in live features
- Trade-off reasoning between hotfix vs rollback vs pausing experiments
- Customer communications and leadership updates without leaking internal data

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: simple bias-mitigating ranking patch
function mitigateBias(ranking, sensitiveFeature) {
  const w = ranking.weights;
  if (sensitiveFeature.confidence > 0.8) {
    w[sensitiveFeature.name] *= 0.75;
  }
  return computeScore(ranking);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate the patch across languages and locales?
- What metrics indicate sustained bias reduction after deployment?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ownership, bias-for-action, and customer-obsession under production risk. It requires concrete triage steps, defined metrics, and clear decision criteria that tie business impact to user experience.

## Key Concepts

- Ownership and incident command
- Real-time metrics and fairness indicators
- Customer impact and transparent communication
- Predefined decision thresholds and post-incident process

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode for rapid rollback decision threshold
function decideRolloutDisaster(metrics, thresholds) {
  if (metrics.groupDisparity > thresholds.disparity) return 'rollback';
  if (metrics.loss > thresholds.loss) return 'patch';
  return 'slow-roll';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate the patch without regressing fairness?
- What monitoring dashboards would you add post-rollback?

